    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001"><term>age of consent</term><meaning>minimum age at which an individual can legally make decisions to engage in sexual behavior</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00002"><term>clique</term><meaning>close group of three to a dozen or so friends</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00003"><term>crowd</term><meaning>large social grouping of many dozens or more members in the social milieu of adolescents</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00004"><term>friendship</term><meaning>intimate, emotionally close relationship between two individuals</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00005"><term>relational aggression</term><meaning>practice of including or excluding others or otherwise threatening a sense of belonging such as by spreading gossip</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00006"><term>romantic relationship</term><meaning>bond psychologically distinct from mere liking and including components of affection, intimacy, exclusivity, and interdependence</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00007"><term>stereotype threat</term><meaning>phenomenon where individuals experience anxiety or fear of confirming negative stereotypes about their social group, which can impair their performance in academic or other achievement-related tasks</meaning></definition>
    </glossary>    
  </document>